- ### Combining
+ ### Combinar

- Two identifiers combine with exclusive-or, and one is inverted with `~`. These are for the
- occasions when a UUID is treated as the bit pattern it is, such as deriving a stable identifier
- from two others:
+ Dos identificadores se combinan con o exclusivo, y uno se invierte con `~`. Esto sirve para las
+ ocasiones en que un UUID se trata como el patrón de bits que es, como al derivar un identificador
+ estable a partir de otros dos:

= from two others:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
+ val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"

= val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
- ```
+ ```

= val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val other = uuid"11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println((id ^ other).text)
+ Out.println((id ^ other).text)

- Out.println((~id).text)
+ Out.println((~id).text)

= Out.println((~id).text)
- ```
+ ```

- [Hashing](hashing.md) derives an identifier from content, and [Randomness](randomness.md)
- controls the source which `Uuid()` draws from.
+ [Hashing](hashing.md) deriva un identificador a partir de un contenido, y
+ [Aleatoriedad](randomness.md) controla la fuente de la que extrae `Uuid()`.
